\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  \cf0 The Lord's my Shepherd, I'll not want;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He makes me down to lie
\par In pastures green; He leadeth me
\par The quiet waters by.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  My soul He doth restore again,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And me to walk doth make
\par Within the paths of righteousness,
\par E'en for His own name's sake.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Yea, though I walk in death's dark vale,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Yet will I fear no ill;
\par For Thou art with me, and Thy rod
\par And staff me comfort still.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. My table Thou hast furnished
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  In presence of my foes;
\par  My head Thou dost with oil anoint,
\par And my cup overflows.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Goodness and mercy all my life
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Shall surely follow me,
\par And in God's house for evermore
\par \pard     My dwelling-place shall be.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

